# Starforge UI — unified & modular

Buttons, inputs, panels, and insert flows must **match existing Starforge chrome** and **reuse shared modules** (Media picker, Forms, Email Manager, etc.). Same job → same UI pattern everywhere.

**Uniformity (hard rule):** Same-type controls must share the **same size, shape, typography, spacing, and color tokens**. All new admin/member UI follows **Layouts / Page Settings / Events** — Starforge colors, Gantry buttons, field shapes. Do not invent tiny inputs, micro labels, or condensed one-off forms.

## Copy shell first (mandatory)

Before writing a new admin settings/list screen:

1. Open the nearest finished page (prefer Events settings or Page Settings).
2. **Copy** structure and classes — do not “approximate”:
   - Nav: `gantry-layouts-nav` + `gantry-layouts-nav-tabs` + `gantry-layouts-nav-tab`
   - Page: `admin-section admin-layouts-full` + `h2` + `lede admin-lede`
   - Settings mosaic: `admin-settings-mosaic` → `page-settings-panel` → `page-settings-panel-head` / `page-settings-panel-body`
   - Fields: `settings-field` (+ `settings-hint`); flags: `settings-field settings-flag`
   - Card actions: `page-settings-actions` bottom-right + `gantry-toolbar-btn` / `gantry-toolbar-btn-save`
   - Save feedback: `useNotifySavedOnOk` + `admin-inline-error` / `admin-inline-ok`
3. If a control does not exist in theme, **extend `core-chrome.css` tokens** — never add module-scoped input sizing CSS.

## Source of truth

| Surface | Tokens / CSS | Prefer these classes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Admin** (`/admin`) | `src/core/admin-theme/themes/starforge-gantry/core-chrome.css` (`--sf-admin-*`, `--sf-*`) | `gantry-btn`, `gantry-btn-primary`, `gantry-toolbar-btn`, `gantry-toolbar-btn-save`, `settings-field`, `page-settings-panel`, `admin-settings-mosaic`, `outlines-create`, `admin-inline-actions` |
| **Payload CMS** (`/cms/admin`) | `…/starforge-gantry/payload-chrome.css` — same tokens; Layouts chrome is the visual reference | Payload widgets themed to SF; shared TipTap/`gantry-*`/`settings-field` when embedded |
| **Public / member account** | `src/app/(frontend)/styles.css` (`:root` `--sf-*`) | Account editors still use `settings-field` + `gantry-btn*` / panel shell when editing |

Prefs (admin): blue-dominated Gantry chrome; orange only on primary Save / rare CTAs; comfortable button size (`--sf-admin-btn-*`); no thin full-width action bars. Payload Publish / Create New = orange; Save Draft = muted toolbar blue — match Layouts.

**Card actions (hard rule):** Cancel / Save / Apply / Delete / Geocode (and siblings) live in the **bottom-right** of the card (`page-settings-actions`, `outlines-create`, `settings-fieldset`, page-settings panel). Use `admin-action-row`, `page-settings-actions`, or `sf-events-form-actions` with `justify-content: flex-end`. Do not left-align or stretch a full-width action strip inside a card. Toolbar / filter / Add+ disclosure bars are not “card actions” — those stay top/inline.

## Same-type = same design

| Control type | Must match |
| --- | --- |
| Text inputs / selects / textareas | `settings-field` height, padding, font-size, border/radius from admin theme — **no** smaller sibling inputs |
| Primary / secondary / toolbar buttons | `gantry-btn` / `gantry-toolbar-btn*` — same min-height as Layouts |
| Labels / helper text | Theme label + `settings-hint` — no tiny uppercase microcopy |
| Fieldsets / cards | `page-settings-panel` / mosaic rhythm |
| Tables / list rows | Existing admin table density |

## Do

- Wrap fields in `settings-field` (label `span` + control) so theme input styles apply.
- Use shared buttons for Create / Save / secondary — same classes as Events, Forms, Email, Page Settings.
- Put card action buttons in the bottom-right corner (see hard rule above).
- **One shared control per concern:** Media → `MediaPicker` / Media library modal; Forms → Form engine; mail → Email Manager. Do not fork a second picker or dialog skin.
- **Same insert UX family:** Rich Editor Image / Gallery / Video all use the inline `sf-rich-editor-media` panel under the toolbar (Video may add Media vs YouTube/Vimeo tabs inside that panel — no separate portal popup).
- Module layout = scoped class (e.g. `.sf-events-manager`) **on top of** shared primitives; override grid/spacing only.
- Match the nearest existing admin page before inventing a new card/dialog language.

## Don’t

- Left-align or full-bleed action rows inside admin cards (always bottom-right).
- Parallel modals/popups for a flow that already has an inline or shared pattern (e.g. video ≠ special dialog when Image/Gallery are inline).
- Raw `<button>` / `<input>` without SF classes next to Gantry/settings chrome.
- One-off colors, radii, paddings that fight `--sf-admin-btn-*` / `--sf-line` / `--sf-primary`.
- Tiny/compact custom inputs, micro labels, or undersized buttons next to normal `settings-field` / `gantry-btn` controls.
- Module-scoped CSS that re-sizes inputs/buttons (fix theme instead).
- New UI-kit skins for admin until the project’s polish wave (prefs).
- Per-module media libraries, field builders, or SMTP UIs.

## Quick check

If two features do the same kind of thing (pick media, edit a field, save, filter), they must share the same component and chrome. If a new control sits next to an existing one and doesn’t match **size, shape, or color** — fix the classes, don’t restyle from scratch. If the page doesn’t look like Events/Layouts settings after a skim — rewrite the shell before shipping.
